{"name":"Cut Ruby","hex":"#a01c2d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cut","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Teutila Cuicatec."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To incise, to cut into the surface of something.\nTo perform an incision on, for example with a knife.\n\nTo divide with a knife, scissors, or another sharp instrument.","To perform an incision on, for example with a knife."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cut"},{"term":"ruby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A clear, deep, red variety of corundum, valued as a precious stone.","A deep red colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a deep, red color; ruby-red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ruby"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ruby","blocks":[{"text":"Ruby is a pinkish-red to blood-red-colored gemstone, a variety of the mineral corundum, consisting of aluminium oxide (α-Al2O3). Ruby is one of the most popular traditional jewelry gems and is very durable. Other varieties of gem-quality corundum are called sapphires, and rubies are also sometimes referred to as \"red sapphires\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Corundum-215330.jpg/330px-Corundum-215330.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruby"},{"title":"Ruby (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Ruby is a color that is a representation of the color of the cut and polished ruby gemstone and is a shade of red or pink."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Ruby_gem.JPG/330px-Ruby_gem.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruby_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Rubis_gisements.jpg/500px-Rubis_gisements.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikime